# kanshi — output layout daemon for wlroots compositors.
#
# kanshi picks the FIRST profile whose `output` lines all match the currently
# connected outputs, applies it, then runs `exec` once. On hotplug it re-runs.
# Output names come from `wlr-randr` — substitute yours where needed.
#
# Coordinates are LOGICAL pixels: origin at top-left of the virtual desktop,
# each output anchored by its top-left corner. To move a monitor "up", lower
# its Y. To move it "left", lower its X. Negative coords are fine.

# kanshi runs each profile's `exec` after a match (initial AND hotplug), so
# the dwl-wallpaper line is what re-spans the wallpaper when a monitor is
# plugged or unplugged.

# ---- laptop only -----------------------------------------------------------
profile laptop {
    output eDP-1 enable mode 1920x1080 position 0,0
    exec ~/.local/bin/dwl-wallpaper ~/.local/share/dwl/wallpaper.png
}

# ---- mine: 3440x1440 ultrawide on top, centered above 1920x1080 laptop -----
# External anchors at 0,0. Laptop centers under it: x = (3440-1920)/2 = 760,
# y = 1440 (just below the external).
profile mine {
    output DP-1  enable mode 3440x1440 position 0,0
    output eDP-1 enable mode 1920x1080 position 760,1440
    exec ~/.local/bin/dwl-wallpaper ~/.local/share/dwl/wallpaper.png
}

# ---- dad: 3440x1440 ultrawide as main, laptop to the LEFT and a bit UP -----
# Main anchors at 1920,200 so there's a 1920-wide column on its left for the
# laptop. Laptop sits at 0,0 (top-left); reducing main's Y makes the laptop
# sit "more above"; increasing it makes the laptop sit "more below".
profile dad {
    output eDP-1 enable mode 1920x1080 position 0,0
    output DP-1  enable mode 3440x1440 position 1920,200
    exec ~/.local/bin/dwl-wallpaper ~/.local/share/dwl/wallpaper.png
}

# Quick reference for tweaking positions:
#
#   Goal                              Change
#   ───────────────────────────────── ───────────────────────────────────────
#   Move external further left        decrease its X
#   Move external further right       increase its X
#   Move external further up          decrease its Y
#   Move external further down        increase its Y
#   Center laptop under wider screen  laptop.X = (extW - lapW) / 2
#   Bottom-align laptop with main     laptop.Y = main.Y + main.H - lap.H
#   Top-align laptop with main        laptop.Y = main.Y
